{title: 400 - I Come With Joy}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #400 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 400}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I [F]come with joy to [C7/E]meet my Lord,
[Bb]Forgiven, loved and [Am]free,
[C]In [Bb]awe [C]and [Dm]wonder [F]to [Gm]recall
[C7]His life laid [Gm]down [C]for [C7]me,
[F]His life laid down for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I [F]come with Christians [C7/E]far and near
[Bb]To find, as all are [Am]fed,
[C]Our [Bb]true [C]community [Gm]of [F]love
[C7]In Christ's communion bread,
[F]In Christ's communion bread.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]As [F]Christ breaks bread for [C7/E]us to share
[Bb]Each proud division [Am]ends.
[C]That [Bb]love [C]that made [Dm]us [F]makes [Gm]us [F]one,
[C7]And strangers [Gm]now [C]are [C7]friends,
[F]And strangers now are friends.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]And [F]thus with joy we [C7/E]meet our Lord.
[Bb]His presence always [Am]near,
[C]Is [Bb]in [C]such [Dm]friendship [F]better known:
[C7]We see and [Gm]praise [C]Him [C7]here,
[F]We see and praise Him here.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Together [F]met, together [C7/E]bound,
[Bb]We'll go our diff'rent [Am]ways,
[C]And [Bb]as [C]His [Dm]people [F]in [Gm]the [F]world,
[C7]We'll live and [Gm]speak [C]His [C7]praise,
[F]We'll live and speak His praise.
{end_of_verse}
